Steps:
[NAV] Navigate to {{FRONT_URL}}/sign-in
[ACT] Fill 'Email': {{USER_EMAIL}}
[ACT] Fill 'Password': {{USER_PASSWORD}}
[ACT] Click 'Sign In'
[WAIT] Wait for redirect after successful login
[ASSERT] Capture /connect/token response in network tab

[NAV] Navigate to {{FRONT_URL}}/sign-in
[ACT] Fill 'Email': {{USER_EMAIL}}
[ACT] Fill 'Password': {{USER_PASSWORD}}
[ACT] Click 'Sign In'
[WAIT] Wait for successful login
[ACT] Capture the access_token from /connect/token response
[ACT] Execute fetch to {{BACK_URL}}/api/platform/settings with Authorization: Bearer {customer_token}
[WAIT] Wait for API response
[ASSERT] API returns 401 or 403
[ACT] Execute fetch to {{BACK_URL}}/api/platform/security/users with Authorization: Bearer {customer_token}
[WAIT] Wait for API response
[ASSERT] API returns 401 or 403
[ACT] Execute fetch to {{BACK_URL}}/api/platform/modules with Authorization: Bearer {customer_token}
[WAIT] Wait for API response

Assertions:
[NAV] /account redirects to login page {OBSERVED}
[NAV] /account/orders redirects to login page {OBSERVED}
[NAV] /checkout redirects an anonymous user to /cart — this store permits guest checkout, so /checkout is NOT behind a login gate {OBSERVED}
[NAV] /company/members redirects to login page {OBSERVED}
[DOM] Login form visible after each redirect to the login page {OBSERVED}
[STATE] No account data visible before authentication {OBSERVED}

Steps:
[HTTP] POST {{BACK_URL}}/connect/token grant_type=password username=@td(TECHFLOW_ADMIN.email) password=@td(TECHFLOW_ADMIN.password) scope=offline_access storeId={{STORE_ID}}
[WAIT] Receive access_token
[HTTP] POST {{BACK_URL}}/graphql Authorization: Bearer <access_token> body: {"query": "{ me { id email } }"}
[WAIT] Receive GraphQL response (expect me.email to match authenticated user)

Assertions:
[STATE] the LOCKED org is never granted as a session context -- a password grant naming @td(ORG_TECHFLOW.platform_id) returns HTTP 200 whose organization_id claim ($LOCKED_REQ_CLAIM) resolves to an ACCESSIBLE org and is NEVER the locked org, so no session is ever scoped to a blocked org (AC3) {OBSERVED} (verified 2026-08-05 on Customer 3.1021.0-pr-312-3aa7: the request was silently substituted to the accessible org with NO refusal code, because a refusal fires only when no accessible org remains -- BL-AUTH-016)
[STATE] BuildRight context login succeeds for the same user and $RESOLVED_CLAIM names the accessible org -- org isolation confirmed: a lock scoped to one organization does not gate the other (AC3) {OBSERVED}
[NETWORK] POST /graphql (me query) returns a valid user id in the BuildRight context and errors[] is empty {OBSERVED}

Cross_Layer_Checks:
[API] POST {{BACK_URL}}/api/customer/organization-memberships/search body {userId: @td(MULTI_ORG_TF_BR.userId)} - at block screen: BuildRight isLocked=true, TechFlow isLocked=false
[API] GET {{BACK_URL}}/api/platform/security/users/@td(MULTI_ORG_TF_BR.userId)/locked - at every HTTP step: must return {locked: false}
[API] At unblock screen: search again - BuildRight isLocked=false
